{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu","id":777164,"title":"Concept for an Ugallu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-30T08:35:51-08:00","id":777164,"title":"Concept for an Ugallu","content":"Could an Ugallu, a Beast who derives their fear from exposure, be based on a creature in a mirror/reflection rather than one from in the air? Reflections are remarkably pervasive in our day to day lives, from windows to monitors to even pools of water (such as bird bathes or even the toilet). Imagine a Nightmare using the fear of every reflective surface around you being the access to allow something else to see you.<br /> <br /> Mind, that might make them a bit more likely to catch onto the Gentry's radar, given reflective surfaces are their thing too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T11:25:04-08:00","id":777259,"title":"","content":"Neat. I don't see why not. Needs Must and Mimir's Wisdom are your go to Atavisms, later Looming Presence and Siren's Treacherous Song. You Are (Not) Alone, Behold, My True Form!, your Nightmares. Maybe snag Epic Fame. I'd lean towards Higher Satiety to stay sharp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T18:40:05-08:00","id":777481,"title":"","content":"Well the exposure is a more important aspect than the air is. So if you want to play a terrifying version of the all seeing mirror there is no issue to that being an Ugallu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:56:01-08:00","id":792281,"title":"","content":"I can see a slightly tweaked version of Shadowed Soul working for being able to go into mirrors. You might need to change it a little though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:19:04-08:00","id":792292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=792281#post792281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see a slightly tweaked version of Shadowed Soul working for being able to go into mirrors. You might need to change it a little though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, one could justify it and say that mirrors, having a backing that is meant to prevent light from getting through, would contain their own shadows...but that's a slippery slope to make before <i>everything</i> has a shadow you can just go into.<br /> <br /> That said, I could see a modified version working pretty well, if more situationally than darkness; seeing through reflections as though they were from another perspective, being able to blend into a reflection and only being ejected when darkness overtook it, being able to jump to any reflection that was within sight of their own...there's a lot that can be done with that. Almost as much as shadows, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:20:45-08:00","id":792295,"title":"","content":"Imagine what you could do after a rainstorm. All those puddles on the road. So many reflections...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:22:08-08:00","id":792296,"title":"","content":"Also, imagine what the Lair would be like. I could imagine something like a maze in which all the walls are silver or glass. I have half a mind to play with this character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:23:31-08:00","id":792298,"title":"","content":"On another note, would the Beast be visible in the mirror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:28:07-08:00","id":792387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=792296#post792296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, imagine what the Lair would be like. I could imagine something like a maze in which all the walls are silver or glass. I have half a mind to play with this character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually my idea for his Lair; Blazing Light and Maze due to it being like a Hall of Mirrors gone insane, maybe Exposed or Mirages due to the Beast being able to see through all the glass his environment is made of but not his foes. Even if foes could get to a vantage point, they'd still have a hard time telling where a reflection actually starts due to them being everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=792298#post792298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, would the Beast be visible in the mirror?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, but perhaps they could hide around objects within said reflection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-24-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:38:56-08:00","id":792392,"title":"","content":"What if the Beast could not only hide himself in the mirrors, but trap others as well? That would probably be a low Satiety or Satiety expenditure effect. Or what about the Beast being able to interact with objects in the real world by interacting with their reflection (like Dr. Facilier's shadow, except with mirrors instead of shadows).<br /> <br /> It would be easy to add Razored to the Lair as well. A maze of broken mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-26-2015, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T15:39:34-08:00","id":792394,"title":"","content":"I'll see what I can do about writing up the mirror Atavism after Christmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:26:59-08:00","id":796951,"title":"","content":"Here it is:<br /> <br /> <b>Through the Looking Glass (Ugallu)</b><br /> Reflections are everywhere in the modern world. Windows, video screens, puddles after rainfall, everywhere. People spend years looking into mirrors, making sure that their face is just right, that they are \u2018beautiful\u2019. People trust mirrors, because when you look into one, you know that what looks back at you is just a reflection.<br /> Except when it\u2019s not. When you look into a mirror and something <i>other </i>looks back. When all of those reflections are the <i>thing\u2019s </i>eyes and every mirror is a door that it can step though. When that happens, where can you hide?<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> None<br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The Beast can step into any reflective surface which is large enough to fit him, entering a world which such Beasts call Mirrorspace. Mirrorspace itself is completely black and empty, the only points of light being the Beast himself and other reflective surfaces, which appear as \u2018windows\u2019 looking out into the real world. These \u2018windows\u2019 are in the same position as they would be in real life (a puddle is on the floor, a bathroom mirror hangs suspended in the air at head height) and show what they would reflect in the real world (the mirror would show a bathroom, the puddle the sky). While the Beast is looking out of a mirror, his reflection appears in its real-world counterpart.<br /> The Beast can only enter and exit Mirrorspace through the same reflection that he used to enter it and always knows the direction and distance to that reflection. Each Beast enters their own Mirrorspace and never encounters another beast within it. Items can be brought into Mirrorspace so long as the beast is holding them. Items <i>can</i> be left in Mirrorspace but only last a number of days equal to the Beast\u2019s (Lair + Composure) before vanishing from Mirrorspace. It is unknown where these items go. The exception to this is within the Lair, where items can remain within a mirror for as long as desired by the Beast.<br /> Beasts can only exit Mirrorspace via the same reflection through which they entered and should that reflection be destroyed the Beast is immediately ejected from Mirrorspace and is subject to the Stunned tilt. A Beast inside Mirrorspace can smash one of the 'windows', destroying its real-life counterpart.<br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As the Beast's hunger grows, he becomes able to access aspects of the Mirrorspace that he otherwise could not. In this case, he gains the ability to exit Mirrorspace through any reflection big enough to fit him. He still has to travel to the mirror physically but is no longer ejected if the point of entry is destroyed.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> With the expenditure of a dot of Satiety, the Beast can bring another with them into Mirrorspace, leaving them trapped there until the Beast retrieves them. Mortals in Mirrorspace do not need food, drink or sleep and do not age. However, after a number of years equal to the Beast's Lair at the time when the victim was trapped, the victim is ejected from Mirrorspace into a random world. They could end up in the mortal world, Arcadia, the Shadow, the Hedge or any other world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:29:16-08:00","id":796953,"title":"","content":"I could imagine this Horror as perhaps a skeletal, hunched-over creature with mirrors for eyes. It never looks directly at you, it looks at reflections of you, seeing you from multiple angles at once. Or it could be a copy of the one looking at it, except more perfected, a better version of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:32:58-08:00","id":797220,"title":"","content":"Very nicely done for the Atavism; funny enough, I've been making a manifestation for Geist called The Hearse (inspired by another two who've made it, but I felt they weren't really balanced all that well), and the Phantasmal Hearse was something similar to this one. Specifically, the user enters a mirror, they're given access to a world that is composed simply of windows that are reflections, and they can be harmed if the mirror they're in is damaged. It's interesting to see someone come up with a similar concept on their own.<br /> <br /> The only question I have is how a Beast can &quot;destroy&quot; a reflection - the problem is that objects that are reflective tend to still stay reflective if they're broken (mirror shards reflecting a person from multiple angles is a popular bit of imagery), and objects like puddles that are naturally reflective can't be &quot;destroyed&quot; easily (even if splashed, the surface reforms). Perhaps the object becomes clouded, or scratched? Maybe blackened by something that affects the material it is composed of (the backing of mirrors becomes corroded, puddles/water become muddied or develop a film, glass is scratched, ect.)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=796953#post796953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could imagine this Horror as perhaps a skeletal, hunched-over creature with mirrors for eyes. It never looks directly at you, it looks at reflections of you, seeing you from multiple angles at once. Or it could be a copy of the one looking at it, except more perfected, a better version of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking something closer to some depictions of Quetzalcoatl - a long, winding serpent with metalic scales that gleam like mirrors and are sharp to the touch. Only in this case, said scales have the patterns of eyes on them, with the scales and the patterns moving like natural eyes would. Unblinking, staring, all seeing. And then it coils around you, seeing you from all positions, making you see <i>yourself</i> from all directions, reflections mirroring each other endlessly. And then it speaks.<br /> <br /> At least, that's the idea. Not sure how well it'd fit in the current incarnation of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T02:23:52-08:00","id":797246,"title":"","content":"With the destruction of the reflections, I was picturing the Beast smashing one of the windows in Mirrorspace and its real-life counterpart breaking as well. The 'windows' look different depending on what kind of reflection it corresponds to. Like, a puddle looks like a pool of quicksilver and can be splashed like one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:45:35-08:00","id":797293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=797220#post797220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been making a manifestation for Geist called The Hearse.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't suppose you could direct me to where you've posed this (if you have) it sounds really interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T12:58:14-08:00","id":797471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/777164-concept-for-an-ugallu?p=797293#post797293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i don't suppose you could direct me to where you've posed this (if you have) it sounds really interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've yet to actually complete the manifestation yet, in spite of how long I've been working on and off on it. Some aspects of it are fleshed out, but others are not. I was inspired when I read of these versions, but the more I read on them, the less balanced they seemed in relation to one another, and in relation to other aspects of being a Sin Eater.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?287815-The-Hearse-%28A-Geist-The-Sin-Eaters-Manifestation%29\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...nifestation%29</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default923f.html?g=posts&amp;t=57622\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default923f.html?g=posts&amp;t=57622\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default923f.html?g=posts&amp;t=57622\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default923f.html?g=posts&amp;t=57622 </a> </di